- timestamp, counter-reset, label, tenant, and metric-identity semantics;
- ingestion authentication, batching, retries, quotas, and cardinality controls;
- how samples are partitioned, aggregated, retained, and queried by time range and labels;
- how raw data, rollups, and downsampling affect query accuracy;
- treatment of duplicate, late, out-of-order, backfilled, and invalid samples;
- behavior under producer bursts, hot tenants, storage pressure, and partial failures; and
