- how each calculation observes a coherent input snapshot;
- how an input change invalidates or incrementally refreshes affected work;
- scheduling, caching, resource isolation, and backpressure across pricers with different costs;
- behavior when inputs are stale or missing or when one pricer is slow, faulty, or unavailable; and
