- how inventory and funds remain consistent under contention, timeouts, cancellation, and partial failure;
- admission control and fairness when demand exceeds supply;
- how capacity and failure isolation protect withdrawals and other Balance Service clients;
- reconciliation, audit, and recovery for ambiguous or incomplete transactions; and
